-- title:
--   Divisorial Hecke ring of J₀(N) embeds in End_ℂS₂(Γ₀(N))
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a non-zero natural number, and write $J_0(N) =$ [`ModularCurve.JZero N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115) for the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` of the modular function field `modularFunctionFieldBar N`. For each prime $\ell$, [`ModularCurve.heckeOperatorBar N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L16) is the $\mathbb Z$-linear endomorphism of $J_0(N)$ underlying `heckeOperatorAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) N ℓ`, which is the correspondence `heckePic0Bar` attached to the data $\alpha,\beta$ when the predicate `HeckeInputsAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) N ℓ` holds and is $0$ otherwise. Two hypotheses are assumed: `HeckeInputsAll N`, namely that for every prime $\ell$ the predicate `HeckeInputsAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) N ℓ` holds (integrality of $\alpha$ and of $\beta$ at level $(N,\ell)$, existence of principal divisors on the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull (N * ℓ)`, finiteness along $\alpha$, and the fundamental identity along $\beta$ together with the norm formula along $\alpha$); and `HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N`, namely that the operators `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` commute pairwise. The conclusion asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\Phi$ from the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb Z}J_0(N)$ generated by the range of `heckeOperatorBar N` into the ring of $\mathbb C$-linear endomorphisms of $\mathrm{CuspForm}(\Gamma_0(N),2)$ such that $\Phi$ is injective and, for every prime $\ell \nmid N$, $\Phi$ sends `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` to the analytic Hecke operator [`CuspForm.heckeTLin 2 ℓ.prop hℓN`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L69), i.e. to $f \mapsto$ `heckeU 2 ℓ f` $+\, f\mid_2 \mathrm{heckeDiagMatrix}\,\ell$.
--
--   This is the comparison between the divisorial Hecke action on $J_0(N)(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ and the classical action of the Hecke operators on weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$, via the cotangent space of the Jacobian; the injectivity is the statement that the geometric Hecke ring acts faithfully on $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$. It is used to transport identities among analytic Hecke operators back to the Jacobian ([`ModularCurve.heckeRelations_jZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.heckeRelations_jZero)) and to produce ring homomorphisms out of the Hecke algebra attached to eigenforms and to Galois representations on $J_0(N)$.
